Subject: winebus: default SDL's MFI joystick backend off on macOS

macOS 26.0 and 27.0 both enumerate Xbox controllers through GameController but
deliver no input from them; SDL's HIDAPI/IOKit path reads the HID reports fine
and keeps rumble. Whisky set SDL_JOYSTICK_MFI=0 on every launch to select it.

Set as a hint at SDL_HINT_DEFAULT priority rather than by putting the variable in
the environment. SDL_GetHint returns the environment ahead of any hint below
SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE, so this is a default the user can still undo with
SDL_JOYSTICK_MFI=1 once a macOS GA release fixes the framework -- the same
"default here, environment still wins" shape as the other launcher constants
moved down in this series, and expressed in SDL's own mechanism rather than by
writing to the process environment behind SDL's back.

diff --git a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
index fbea0cb00b9..cbc29006ab4 100644
--- a/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
+++ b/dlls/winebus.sys/bus_sdl.c
@@ -1181,6 +1181,13 @@ NTSTATUS sdl_bus_init(void *args)
     pSDL_SetHintWithPriority("SteamVirtualGamepadInfo", "", SDL_HINT_OVERRIDE);
     unsetenv("SteamVirtualGamepadInfo");
 
+    /* Skip SDL's GameController backend on macOS: 26.0 and 27.0 enumerate Xbox
+     * pads through it but deliver no input, while HIDAPI/IOKit reads the reports
+     * and keeps rumble. SDL_HINT_DEFAULT rather than OVERRIDE, because SDL_GetHint
+     * returns the environment ahead of any lower-priority hint -- so this is a
+     * default that SDL_JOYSTICK_MFI=1 can still undo when GA fixes the framework. */
+    pSDL_SetHintWithPriority(SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_MFI, "0", SDL_HINT_DEFAULT);
+
     if (pSDL_Init(SDL_INIT_GAMECONTROLLER | SDL_INIT_HAPTIC) < 0)
     {
         ERR("could not init SDL: %s\n", pSDL_GetError());
